      "body": "This PR adds a new parameter to `read_csv_auto`, the  `auto_type_candidates` that receives a list of types.\r\n\r\ne.g.,\r\n\r\n```sql \r\nSELECT * FROM read_csv_auto ('csv_file.csv', auto_type_candidates=['FLOAT','VARCHAR']); \r\n```\r\n\r\nWill only automatically test `FLOAT` and `VARCHAR` as possible columns in the CSV File.\r\n\r\nBy default, `auto_type_candidates` will always attempt to detect the following column types: \r\n```\r\nVARCHAR\r\nTIMESTAMP\r\nDATE\r\nTIME\r\nDOUBLE\r\nBIGINT\r\nBOOLEAN\r\nSQLNULL \r\n```\r\n\r\nIf a column has a type that can not be deduced to one of the set `auto_type_candidates`, an error is thrown.\r\n\r\nAlso important to notice that mistyping might be more frequent with smaller sample sizes if more specialized types are used (e.g., TINYINT might be detected to a column, because the sample did not pick an Integer).\r\n\r\nFix: #6742 ",
      "reactions": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/issues/6756/reactions",
        "total_count": 0,
        "+1": 0,
        "-1": 0,
        "laugh": 0,
        "hooray": 0,
        "confused": 0,
